Final 5-Minute Pitch Script (Optimized & Integrated)
[Slide 1: Title Slide] (0:00 - 0:35)
"Hello everyone, and thank you for being here. I’m proud to introduce OurHome—a platform where structured data telemetry and machine learning meet profound 
human empathy. Engineered to support individuals managing Major Depressive Disorder, Anxiety, and ADHD, OurHome is built to fulfill SDG 3 (Good Health and 
Well-being) and SDG 10 (Reduced Inequalities) by democratizing a pressure-free, intelligent mental health support ecosystem."

[Slide 2: The Philosophy, Distance & SDGs] (0:35 - 1:25)
"To understand OurHome, we must first address a universal human challenge: supporting loved ones who are physically not by our side. Whether it’s a partner 
across cities, a family member far away, or a friend going through burnout, distance breaks natural bonds.
When we try to bridge this gap with standard communication, it often backfires. For someone experiencing executive dysfunction, an incoming text asking 'Did 
you eat?' or 'How are you?' demands an active cognitive response. It induces guilt, pressure, and social withdrawal.
That’s why we adopted the sociological concepts of 'Affective Presencing' and virtual 'Body Doubling'. In physical psychology, sharing a quiet room creates 
safety. Our mission was to digitize that psychological safety net across distance, allowing us to be there for each other without demanding energy."

[Slide 3: Structured Interaction Data & Sources] (1:25 - 2:15)
"To achieve this, OurHome functions as a smart data engine. The application collects three layers of non-invasive, structured time-series telemetry:
First, Routine Kinetics: Timestamped logs of micro-habit completions, tracking when and how frequently a user interacts with basic self-care.
Second, Ambient Engagement: Tracking the duration and frequency of silent profile views—quantifying when a user opens the app simply to look at their partner's 
routine as a form of digital proximity.
Third, Micro-Cue Telemetry: Analyzing the frequency and clustering of non-verbal interactions, such as the one-click 'Send Hug' floating animations.

When it comes to our data sources, we look beyond just basic application clicks. While our primary source is the real-time, in-app telemetry captured via 
Firebase—such as routine kinetics and ambient view durations—we also integrate secondary behavioral benchmarks. We utilize anonymized Ecological Momentary 
Assessment (EMA) open datasets from mental health research to validate our predictive models. Furthermore, looking at our roadmap within the Samsung ecosystem, 
we plan to incorporate passive physiological telemetry from wearables like Galaxy Watches—such as heart rate variability and sleep tracking—to make our anomaly 
detection even more precise, all while maintaining absolute user privacy."

[Slide 4: Machine Learning Implementation] (2:15 - 3:15)
"This brings us to the core technical innovation of OurHome: how we utilize Machine Learning.
Because our input data consists of structured time-series metrics rather than unstructured video or audio, we implement robust, highly interpretable classifiers
like Random Forest and XGBoost.
The AI model operates invisibly behind the scenes in three distinct ways:

Anomaly & Energy Inference: By analyzing temporal shifts—such as a sudden decrease in habit logging rates or a drop in ambient view frequencies—the model detects 
latent indicators of high cognitive load or depressive phases.

Adaptive UI Scaling: When the model infers a low-energy window, it instructs the frontend to dynamically scale down UI density. It hides complex features and 
surfaces only fundamental, 1-click micro-steps, preventing cognitive overwhelm.

Algorithmic Nudging: The model computes the optimal psychological window for a distant caregiver or partner to send a silent support cue, ensuring empathy arrives
precisely when needed without triggering anxiety."

[Slide 5: The Human Interface] (3:15 - 4:05)
"All of this complex AI processing translates into a beautifully simple, Zero-Expectation UX. Divided into Personal and Shared spaces, the interface bypasses 
mental fatigue entirely through pre-populated 1-click micro-presets. The user doesn’t have to type or think of tasks from scratch. Powered by real-time Firebase 
synchronization, when one user checks off a step, the partner receives immediate, silent visual confirmation miles away. We are connected, without saying a word."

[Slide 6: Ethical & Clinical Boundaries] (4:05 - 5:00)
"Finally, our ethical architecture is non-negotiable. Our data pipeline is fully GDPR-compliant, utilizing strict anonymization with zero Personally Identifiable 
Information (PII) exposed to the ML engine. We intentionally avoid clinical diagnostic labeling to prevent reinforcing psychological stigma.
OurHome proves that advanced machine learning should not be used to demand corporate productivity, but to protect human vulnerability and foster genuine connection. 
Thank you for your time."
